# Example machine-local settings for refresh.sh.
#
# Copy to ~/.workbuddy-ai/vps-deals.env (or point VPS_DEALS_ENV at it) and edit.
# refresh.sh reads it if it exists and otherwise falls back to portable defaults,
# so none of this needs to be — or should be — committed.
#
# Everything here is overridable by environment variable too.

# Interpreter and wrangler. Defaults are `python3` and `npx wrangler`.
# PY=C:/Python313/python.exe
# WRANGLER=npx wrangler

# Where the Cloudflare credential lives. refresh.sh reads api_token.txt from
# this directory; the token is never read from the repo.
# CF_DIR=$HOME/.workbuddy-ai/cloudflare

# Required for publishing. Without it refresh.sh exits 1 rather than deploying.
# CF_ACCOUNT=your-cloudflare-account-id

# The Pages project to deploy to. Defaults to vps-deals-radar.
# CF_PROJECT=vps-deals-radar

# Set to 1 to scrape, build and commit without publishing.
# SKIP_DEPLOY=1
